{"name":"Marsh Fog","hex":"#c6d8c7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"marsh","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An area of low, wet land, often with tall grass or herbaceous plants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marsh"},{"term":"fog","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thick cloud that forms near the ground; the obscurity of such a cloud.","A mist or film clouding a surface."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To become covered with or as if with fog.","To become obscured in condensation or water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fog"}],"entries":[{"title":"Marsh","blocks":[{"text":"In ecology, a marsh is a wetland that is dominated by herbaceous plants rather than by woody plants. More in general, the word can be used for any low-lying and seasonally waterlogged terrain. In Europe and in agricultural literature, low-lying meadows that require draining and embanked polderlands are also referred to as marshes or marshland."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Meadowlands_Lyndhurst.jpg/330px-Meadowlands_Lyndhurst.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marsh","wikidata":"Q30198"},{"title":"Fog","blocks":[{"text":"Fog is a visible aerosol consisting of tiny water droplets or ice crystals held in the air near the Earth's surface. Fog can be considered a type of low-lying cloud usually resembling stratus and is heavily influenced by nearby bodies of water, topography, and wind conditions. In turn, fog affects many human activities, such as shipping, travel, and warfare. Recent atmospheric research indicates that fog also functions as an active aquatic ecosystem. Fog droplets harbor microbiomes where bacteria actively grow, divide, and interact with atmospheric chemistry."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/A_foggy_winter_morning.jpg/330px-A_foggy_winter_morning.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fog","wikidata":"Q37477"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Coastal_marsh_profile.png/500px-Coastal_marsh_profile.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Coastal_marsh_profile.png/500px-Coastal_marsh_profile.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Marsh in shallow water on a lakeshore","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACoastal_marsh_profile.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Water_Lily_-_geograph.org.uk_-_483063.jpg/500px-Water_Lily_-_geograph.org.uk_-_483063.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Water_Lily_-_geograph.org.uk_-_483063.jpg/500px-Water_Lily_-_geograph.org.uk_-_483063.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"White water lilies are a typical marsh plant in European areas of deeper water.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWater_Lily_-_geograph.org.uk_-_483063.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Xanthocephalus_xanthocephalus_-100_Mile_House%2C_British_Columbia%2C_Canada_-male-8.jpg/500px-Xanthocephalus_xanthocephalus_-100_Mile_House%2C_British_Columbia%2C_Canada_-male-8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Xanthocephalus_xanthocephalus_-100_Mile_House%2C_British_Columbia%2C_Canada_-male-8.jpg/500px-Xanthocephalus_xanthocephalus_-100_Mile_House%2C_British_Columbia%2C_Canada_-male-8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Many kinds of birds nest in marshes; this one is a yel